{
  "name": "How to get your content cited by voice assistants",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1: Getting your business recommended by voice assistants like Siri, Al…",
      "text": "Getting your business recommended by voice assistants like Siri, Alexa, or Google Assistant is a game-changer, but it requires a slightly different approach than text-based AI search. When someone asks a question out loud, they typically get *one* spoken answer, not a list of ten. That's why it's so important to optimize for this 'higher stakes' environment.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 2: The key here is 'speakable schema.' This special markup tells voice…",
      "text": "The key here is 'speakable schema.' This special markup tells voice assistants exactly which parts of your content are designed to be read aloud as direct, concise answers. Without it, the assistant has to guess, and that's a gamble you don't want to take. Your content needs to be short, clear, and self-contained, specifically crafted for a spoken response. Imagine someone asking, 'Hey, find me a good plumber near me.' If your site has speakable schema for a direct answer about your plumbing services and location, you're in the running. If it doesn't, you're likely out of the conversation.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 2
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 3: Start by listing the 'near me' and scenario-based questions your id…",
      "text": "Start by listing the 'near me' and scenario-based questions your ideal clients would ask out loud. For each, draft a super-concise, direct answer, ideally just a sentence or two. Think about what a voice assistant could realistically read without losing the user's attention. Gather your exact business name, address, phone number, and hours – consistency is key. Ensure these details are present and correct across your website and Google Business Profile. If you're dealing with multiple locations or complex services, getting professional guidance on implementing speakable schema and structuring your answers correctly can make a huge difference, ensuring your business is the one spoken about.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 3
    }
  ],
  "@type": "HowTo",
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "speakable": {
    "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
    "cssSelector": [
      "h1",
      ".howto-step",
      "[itemprop=\"step\"]"
    ]
  },
